Selecting a kinematics from G-code with G12.1 and G13.1.

The machine stands in a pose where the two kinematics disagree about
where it is, which is the only place the codes can be tested: a switch
that changes nothing proves nothing.  From there the test checks that the
block after the switch is planned in the kinematics that runs it, that
the selection reaches the motion controller and the interpreter, that a
negative P word and a kinematics the module does not provide are refused,
that G13.1 cancels to the identity kinematics the module declares (type 1
here, not 0), and that G13.1 in an ON_ABORT_COMMAND routine does not
swallow the rest of the routine.
